{"@context":{"lean":"lean:","block":"block:","imports":{"@type":"@id"}},"@graph":[{"@id":"lean:module:QOU.Observations.CrossingDiscriminantThetaFree","@type":"LeanModule","name":"QOU.Observations.CrossingDiscriminantThetaFree","imports":["lean:module:Init","lean:module:Mathlib.Analysis.SpecialFunctions.Complex.Circle","lean:module:Mathlib.Tactic.FieldSimp","lean:module:Mathlib.Tactic.Ring"],"declarations":6,"chunks":1},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Observations.CrossingDiscriminantThetaFree.crossingDisc_pos_of_one_lt","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Observations.CrossingDiscriminantThetaFree.crossingDisc_pos_of_one_lt","kind":"theorem","line":97,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Observations/CrossingDiscriminantThetaFree.lean#L97-L105","doc":"For a substrate with `|q| > 1` the discriminant is **strictly positive** —\nso the `q ↔ q⁻¹` asymmetry the mirror introduces is not merely nonzero at some\norders, it never vanishes.  This is the direction that does work: no choice of\nphase can make the two crossing energies agree in magnitude. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Observations.CrossingDiscriminantThetaFree.crossingDisc_norm_theta_free","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Observations.CrossingDiscriminantThetaFree.crossingDisc_norm_theta_free","kind":"theorem","line":74,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Observations/CrossingDiscriminantThetaFree.lean#L74-L95","doc":"**The θ-free statement, with the phase present and explicit.**  Write the\nparticle's crossing energy as `n·q` and the mirror's as `−n/q` with\n`q = r·e^{iθ}` — which is `def:crossing-energy` on an all-positive braid\ntogether with `prop:antiparticle-crossing-reversal` item 2.  Then the\ndiscriminant of their norms equals `(r² − 1)/(r² + 1)` **for every** `θ`.\n\n`θ` is bound on the left and absent on the right: that is the refutation of the\n`O(θ²)` claim, and it is not an approximation. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Observations.CrossingDiscriminantThetaFree.disc_eq_tanh_log","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Observations.CrossingDiscriminantThetaFree.disc_eq_tanh_log","kind":"theorem","line":66,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Observations/CrossingDiscriminantThetaFree.lean#L66-L72","doc":"`(r² − 1)/(r² + 1) = tanh (log r)` — the closed form the probe reports. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Observations.CrossingDiscriminantThetaFree.crossingDisc_scale_inv","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Observations.CrossingDiscriminantThetaFree.crossingDisc_scale_inv","kind":"theorem","line":52,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Observations/CrossingDiscriminantThetaFree.lean#L52-L64","doc":"**The corpus's reading.**  Under `prop:antiparticle-crossing-reversal` the\nmirror sends the modulus `c·r` to `c/r`.  The discriminant is then\n`(r² − 1)/(r² + 1)` — and note the overall factor `c` **cancels**, so it is\nindependent of the crossing count as well as of the phase. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Observations.CrossingDiscriminantThetaFree.crossingDisc_self","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Observations.CrossingDiscriminantThetaFree.crossingDisc_self","kind":"theorem","line":44,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Observations/CrossingDiscriminantThetaFree.lean#L44-L50","doc":"**Item 1's reading, carried to its conclusion.**  `conj:complex-chirality-\nrotation` item 1 says the mirror multiplies `S_c` by `e^{-i n_c θ}` where the\nparticle carries `e^{+i n_c θ}`.  A phase has modulus one, so the two moduli\ncoincide and the discriminant is **identically zero** — to all orders, not to\nfirst.  The block's own item 1 therefore contradicts its own `O(θ²)`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Observations.CrossingDiscriminantThetaFree.crossingDisc","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Observations.CrossingDiscriminantThetaFree.crossingDisc","kind":"def","line":39,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Observations/CrossingDiscriminantThetaFree.lean#L39-L42","doc":"The discriminant the block forms, as a function of the two **moduli**.\nThis is the whole point: it is a function of `‖·‖` alone, so it is blind to\nevery phase by construction. ","signatureChunk":0}]}